<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Jordan</h1><p class="st-meta">1946 CE – present · capital Amman</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Hashemite kingdom east of the Jordan, carved from the Arab revolt's inheritance and steered through war after war by its long-reigning kings.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Abdullah ibn Hussein, son of the sharif of Mecca, established himself at Amman in 1921, and Britain recognised the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-transjordan">Emirate of Transjordan</a> alongside its Palestine mandate. Full independence came in 1946, and after the war of 1948 Abdullah annexed the West Bank and took the title King of Jordan.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The monarchy survived Abdullah's assassination in 1951; his grandson Hussein reigned from 1952 to 1999 through coup attempts, the loss of the West Bank in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/six-day-war">Six-Day War</a> and civil war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine-liberation-organization">PLO</a> in 1970. Waves of Palestinian, Iraqi and Syrian refugees made and remade Jordanian society around a resource-poor but strategically indispensable state.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Jordan renounced its claim to the West Bank in 1988 and signed peace with Israel in 1994. Under Abdullah II the kingdom remains a hub of regional diplomacy and a refuge amid its neighbours' wars.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1946 CE – present"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:98.43%;width:1.57%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1946 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Amman</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hashemite kings of Jordan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (majority), Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan, Hashemite Kingdom of Transjordan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1986&amp;focus=jordan" aria-label="Jordan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5605 1015 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Jordan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5925 1271L5925 1271"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5925 1271h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5925 1271h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5925 1271h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1986&amp;focus=jordan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
